betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACAw.name=Genetic Template
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACAw.desc=Templates are used to combine multiple gene samples into one large batch. It can be used to apply multiple traits at once, but you can also replicate a bee from liquid DNA and protein, if you manage to fill all 13 traits in one template. These templates can also be copied, just like the small samples.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACBA.name=A Rather Cruel Disposal
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACBA.desc=You'll probably end up with a lot of excess drones while doing bees. (Or saplings if you do trees). Instead of throwing them away, you could also turn them into... something useful.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACBQ.name=Arnie's Blender
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACBQ.desc=They say breakfast is the most important meal of the day. This machine turns raw meat into liquid protein, which is used to create bees from scratch. Which has §oabsolutely nothing§r to do with breakfast.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACBg.name=And There Shall be Light
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACBg.desc=Out of princesses to inject traits to? Too lazy to find hives and get more bees? Not a problem. With this nifty little device, you can use a ton of power, liquid DNA and protein to create any bee you wish to have. The only drawback is: All bees will be ignoble, which means they will die after a random amount of cycles after 90.%n%nOf course, there's an upgrade for the industrial apiary to deal with that
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACBw.name=Only the Best: Temperature
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACBw.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available.%n%n[note]None is for testing jubilant state, while 3 is what you'll have on most of the time. You can hit all temp requirements with 3 if you work in a normal temp area. You can go up to 5 if you use the acclimatiser and want nether bees working in an icy area for some reason.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACCA.name=Only the Best: Humidity
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACCA.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available.%n%n[note]None is for testing jubilant state, while 2 is what you'll have on most of the time. 3+ don't do anything as the range doesn't go that high.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACCQ.name=Only the Best: Fertility
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACCQ.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available. Bees bees everywhere!%n%n[note]F4 is great while breeding bees, but F1 is what you want to use when producing stuff.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACCg.name=Highend species: Draconic
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACCg.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACCw.name=Highend species: Doctoral
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACCw.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACDA.name=Only the Best: Speed Blinding
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACDA.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available. Buzz buzz buzz, working hard and really buzzing!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACDQ.name=Highend species: Silicon
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACDQ.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACDg.name=Only the Best: Rain
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACDg.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available. Beekeeping in the rain! Make sure to keep your GT machines covered!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACDw.name=Only the Best: Day and Night
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACDw.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available. Bee working day and night, all night and all day long!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACEA.name=Only the Best: Cave
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACEA.desc=On your way to awesome bees, you have to collect only the best traits available. Bees with Cave can work in housing that is covered - by more housing!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAF7A.name=Breeding Bees Into Oblivion
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAF7A.desc=If bee breeding is a dice game, then these are the biggest factors you'd control to win:%n%n1. Fertility: How many dice you can roll each turn.%n2. Mutation Rate: How good of a roll you need to make.%n3. Lifespan: How often you can play the game.%n%nThe Oblivion Frame dramatically helps with #3 by reducing the bee's lifespan to the point that you can play the breeding dice game in one "tick" of 27.5 seconds. A bee with the "Shortest" lifespan trait cycles for 10 ticks (275 seconds), so you'd minimally cut the cycle by a whole order of magnitude!%n%nYou can find Oblivion Frames in Stronghold libraries. This is how you can get them in the early game for very aggressive bee breeding. Later, you can make them from Dragon Eggs. These frames are very precious and you don't want their durability to run out. A typical repair method is to use a Thaumic Restorer on them.%n%n§oWait, to find a Stronghold reliably, I need some Eyes of Ender, and that's an HV-tier Chemical Reactor recipe!§r If you happen to have a Large Chemical Reactor, remember that it overclocks perfectly, so you can crank er' up with a bunch of MV-tier Energy Input Hatches.%n%n§nThe Oblivion Bee Meta%n§r%nThe oblivion bee meta can be enough to breed most bees quickly. You could do the whole bee breeding quest line with it, but you can ultimately improve on it with Alvearies and genetic modification. What you need for this meta is:%n%n1. An Apiary%n2. An Oblivion Frame%n3. Some way to repair the frame (typically: thaumic restorer)%n4. A Beealyzer and a lot of honey%n%nThis is a hands-on process. You don't automatically send the princess and drones back through because you need to watch the oblivion frame's durability. You inspect all the offspring bees after each cycle and hand-pick which to try next after a pass through the Beealyzer.%n%nYou can accelerate the Apiary with a World Accelerator. [warn]Be sure to protect the World Accelerator and supporting equipment from rain![/warn] You can use glass or a breakable clear glass so the Apiary can still see the sky while the World Accelerator is protected. If you need to use batteries, you can use a State Cell to draw out a button pulse to the world accelerator so it runs juuust long enough for an accelerated cycle.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIKg.name=Fastest Way to Get There
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIKg.desc=A GT++ Mutagenic frame will get your bees to their final destination faster than you can blink. Just remember to wear your rubber suit while making it!%n%n[note]These will break in the alveary before they take effect since their durability is under 6. So you can only get to 125x, but I think that's enough, don't you?[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAILw.name=Genepool
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAILw.desc=You will need to feed Raw DNA into a Polymerizer to prime your gene samples for injection into Larvae. The Genepool eats Enzyme and guzzles Ethanol in order to produce more Raw DNA than you could ever find even in a public gas station's restroom.%n%nIt is basically a chipper shredder for your leftover drones. You were hoarding them because you might need them some day, right? Today's that day! Whatever you put in here is going to go bye-bye. Make sure you keep some of your different drones around just in case.%n%nIt will also take saplings, flowers, and any excess Larvae you should be pumping out by now for modification and hatching.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIMA.name=Isolator
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIMA.desc=The Isolator will take Ethanol and Enzyme to extract a single gene from a candidate bee. Sometimes it gets hungry and eats the bee too. Don't feed it any bees you won't mind getting destroyed!%n%nYou must provide a Blank Sequence to store the output gene. This will be stored with a "faint" level of strength that can be sequenced slowly, or made stronger to be sequenced faster by passing the sequence through a Polymerizer.%n%nThe exact gene you get from the bee is going to be a random choice from that bee's genome. You won't know what it is until you run it through the Sequencer. It will then be accessible forever in the Gene Database.%n%nYou can wind up isolating the same gene from the same bee multiple times. It's just bad luck. They won't be isolated in any particular order.%n%nThe Sequencer will drain the container back into a Blank Sequence, so you can feed them back into the Isolator. You only ever need to make a few Blank Sequences because you can just loop like this indefinitely. If, however, you have a sequenced gene and want to make it blank again immediately, then just run it through your smelting/furnace device of choice.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIMQ.name=Sequencer
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIMQ.desc=After obtaining a DNA Sequence with the gene that you wish, it must be placed in the Sequencer. This uses Fluorescent Dye to determine the correct sequence, and when completed, logs the discovery. The important thing here is that §nthe discovery goes to the person who placed the machine.%n%n§rThis process takes §l16 minutes§r! If the gene has been passed through a Polymeriser beforehand, it'll speed it up to only 4 minutes. You could also hug the machine with World Accelerators in Tile Entity mode to speed it up further.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIMg.name=Polymeriser
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIMg.desc=The Polymeriser is necessary to turn Serum into something you can actually inject into a Larvae. It has a bonus use of strengthening an isolated gene so it can be sequenced faster by a factor of 4x.%n%nThe Polymeriser requires Raw DNA and Polymerising Bacteria. Raw DNA is obtained from the Genepool, and Polymerising Bacteria is made from incubating bacteria with bone meal. Gold nuggets can be used as a catalyst to speed up the process. You can also make more Polymerising Bacteria by feeding it back into an Incubator with Growth Medium.%n%nWhen using the Polymeriser to prepare some Serum for a Larvae, the result will have a number of "charges." In other words, you get multiple uses out of it. This is nice because you are going to need to make a bunch of drones if you are trying to get all those traits to stick. Remember that you cannot use this process to modify a princess or queen directly! If you are satisfied before you use up all the Serum, you can recycle it by passing it through a smelter/furnace of your choice.%n%nIt takes two minutes to polymerise stuff. If you already use a World Accelerator for sequencing, then the Polymeriser would also benefit from cuddling up with that accelerator on another side.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIMw.name=Gene Database
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIMw.desc=Discovered genes are logged into the Gene Database. This handheld device lists all genes by the type of organism they apply to.%n%n§oThis device requires an EV circuit! Of all the things in the Binnie's Genetics line, it has the most technologically sophisticated requirement!%n§r%nUse an Empty Serum Vial or Empty Serum Array on the different discovered traits to prepare a cocktail you want to inject into a Larvae. If you misclick, you can just click on the one you wanted without consequence.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAINg.name=Registry
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAINg.desc=The Registry combines the existing four databases into a new sleek browser to allow the properties, mutations and genes of all discovered bees, trees, butterflies and flowers.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAINw.name=Droning On
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAINw.desc=§n§rFinally! You can hack bees*! You have two choices, and you will only ever need one. Either way you go, you will hatch the modified drone using an Incubator that's been loaded with Bacteria Vector afterwards.%n%nBoth scale their requirements by the number of genes you intend to apply to a single Larvae.%n%n§nThe Inoculator§r%n%nRun Time: 10 minutes per gene%nRF Cost: 600,000 RF per gene%nRF/t: 50%nBacteria Vector: 15 mB per gene.%n%nThis one has a lower power and recipe cost at the expense of needing Bacteria Vector, created by incubating Bacteria and Blaze Powder, to transfer the gene into organisms. The consumption for Bacteria Vector is quite low.%n%nIt is also §oslooooow§... %n§r%n§nThe Splicer§r%n%nRun Time: 1 minute per gene%nRF Cost: 12,000,000 RF per gene%nRF/t: §l1,000%n§r%nThe Splicer is much like the Inoculator in function, however it has the benefit of not requiring any liquid. Its power consumption is terrifying compared to the Inoculator, but overall it only consumes twice the RF despite gobbling it much faster.%n%n*or trees and flowers via their pollen, or butterflies via their caterpillars.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIzw.name=Keep Calm and Bee On
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIzw.desc=This frame will let your bees last longer, and also increase the territory to help with tree breeding.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAK0A.name=Bee Slurry, the Breakfast of, Well, Weirdos
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAK0A.desc=Why would you even need this?
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKuw.name=A Bag for Butterflies, §oyawn§r
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKuw.desc=I'm not sure this has any utility value since the butterflies are going to all be in chunkloaded areas, and thus near your base, but feel free to make it anyway.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKvA.name=Only the Best: Tree Breeding
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKvA.desc=For those who love Forestry trees.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKvQ.name=Only the Worst: Trees Suck!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKvQ.desc=For those who don't like flowers or trees :(.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAM1A.name=IAADDS
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAM1A.desc=Aka the Mega Apiary.%n%nIt has three primary modes (change with screwdriver) and two operation modes (change with shift+screwdriver):%n%nINPUT MODE: Does not take power. Put your queens in the input bus to put them in the internal buffer.%n%nOUTPUT MODE: Does not take power. Will give your bees back to the output bus.%n%nOPERATING MODE - NORMAL: The processing time is 5 seconds. Uses 1 Amp LuV per queen. All bees are affected by 64x acceleration and 8 Production Upgrades as well as a Genetic Stabilizer Upgrade. The IAADDS also simulates a perfect environment for all bees.%n%nYou can provide royal jelly to increase the outputs. 1 royal jelly grants 5%% bonus per bee. They will be consumed on each start of operation and be applied to that operation only. The maximum bonus is 200%%. The normal bee stats still apply of course, though the IAADDS is able to provide a perfect environment for any bee.%n%nOPERATING MODE - SWARMER: In this mode you can only insert 1 queen. The IAADDS will then slowly produce ignoble princesses for 100 royal jelly per operation. The base processing time is 1 minute but you can overclock this process. The base usage is 1 Amp IV.%n%n[note]Yes you need thousands of queens, not princesses.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.FLhv4l1HSSmaLiwukzMVSg.name=Pollen Collection Kit
betterquesting.quest.FLhv4l1HSSmaLiwukzMVSg.desc=The easy way to get some pollen, just right-click on leaves. The Pollen Collection Kits are one-time use though, so maybe make a few.
betterquesting.quest.Hhjp0qVoTpGwa7tXdFxDIg.name=Living It Larvae
betterquesting.quest.Hhjp0qVoTpGwa7tXdFxDIg.desc=To play with Binnie's Genetics with bees, you'll need some Larvae, and a Hatchery block inside an Alveary is the only way to make them. There's a little side perk for having them: they produce at a much faster rate than you'd get from any one species' drones. Those leftovers can feed into the Gene Pool for extra raw DNA. Just remember to keep a few Larvae on standby for the actual genetic modification!%n%nThe bee you use in the Alveary should be whatever you intend to modify. It can be any kind if you intend to overwrite all the traits, but you probably should have it either be:%n%n1. Some new species which will have everything else overwritten.%n2. Some existing superbee that you want to switch to a new species.%n%nThe Larvae will eventually be hatched in an Incubator into a modified drone based on whatever genetic traits you have inserted into it.
betterquesting.quest.TXoGYz4yQZa_Ei-7Xmmt-A.name=Fluorescent Dye
betterquesting.quest.TXoGYz4yQZa_Ei-7Xmmt-A.desc=Here is another one requiring ingredients you'll want to passively generate. The Sequencer needs one (1) Fluorescent Dye per gene it sequences. Each one is made from one of each tossed into a Mixer:%n%n* redstone%n* glowstone%n* orange dye%n* yellow dye%n* molten blaze (from blaze powder)%n%nGiven how many bees you'll end up sequencing to get all the key genes you want, expect to need at least some hundreds or even thousands of these. Yes, there are only so many actual genes, but you're going to be hitting duplicates.
betterquesting.quest.VPMAIP9xRoqjJKeuED9cgw.name=Enzyme on The Mind
betterquesting.quest.VPMAIP9xRoqjJKeuED9cgw.desc=Both the Genepool and the Isolator will require Enzyme. This is a resource you will want to passively generate for continuous gene research. It will require Bacteria and sugar. Bacteria can be created from (fluid) Growth Medium and Wheat in an Incubator. If you then have a bunch of Growth Medium, you can keep using that instead to stretch out that Bacteria forever. It's kind of like a sourdough starter.%n%nFor sugar, there's plenty of ways to passively generate that, including from bees!
betterquesting.quest.t4W99zCeT8qQIqbNyaCE_Q.name=Growth Medium
betterquesting.quest.t4W99zCeT8qQIqbNyaCE_Q.desc=The Binnie's Genetics machines will rely on Growth Medium in either a little, or a lot. If you can't make too much of it, then you'll need to rely on other passive generation to keep the machines constantly supplied for researching genes. If you can make a lot of Growth Medium, then you can use it in a closed loop in Incubators to duplicate some of the mod's resources you have previously produced just once.%n%nIt requires:%n* Sugar: The easy one here, and remember multiple bee species can produce it too.%n* Bones (whole bones, not meal): mob farm, animal traps, goofy conversions.%n* Wood Ash: Smelt some saplings.%n* Mulch: There are a lot of ways to do this, but consider Peat bees since you're already going for the bees.%n%nThis quest is just a little nudge that you should passively produce Growth Medium, which means being able to passively produce all of these ingredients.
betterquesting.quest.0pW02AJaQL-_IffLjNEqaQ.desc=The MakeMake bee allows you to obtain resources from MakeMake.%n%n[note]MakeMake dust provides Infinity and niobium. Why not let bees handle it?[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABYQ.desc=An iridium bee. You can actually get small amounts of pure osmium and iridium from its combs.%n%n[note]With these combs and the uranium ones you can now make climate control units for modules in your industrial apiary![/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABYw.desc=You made it all the way to the Neutronium Bee! Wow!%n%nThe Neutronium Combs can not just lighten the burden on your smelting setup, you can also use them to finally make the Advanced Mutatron.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABZg.desc=A naquadah bee. It doesn't let you avoid the naquadah line, but if you have sufficient technology you can make a Mutatron now!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABaw.desc=There is whole swarm of gas producing bees. Let's breed just one of them here. Check out NEI to see all the options you can aim for.%n%n[note]The Xenon Bee might be the most useful one. You can use it for Void Miners and potentially smelting time reductions.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABdA.name=End Dust
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABdA.desc=A bit of a misnamed bee. What it really gives you is Ender Goo and End Powder.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABhg.desc=This bee multiplies all sources of Indium by 3x.%nThe Indium bee is available in LuV, or in IV with the help of magic.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABiw.desc=The Dragon Blood Bee is a lot of effort to obtain but quite handy for hypogen in late game.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAI5A.name=Smouldering
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAI5A.desc=Smouldering drones will spawn blazes, and make Blaze Rods as their specialty. Breed the drones with your template princesses so you can prevent the harmful effects from destroying your base. Also, their Hellish temperature and Normal humidity requirements are interesting - use an Acclimatiser from Genetics to make the bee tolerant or other methods to adjust the biome. Must be bred in the Nether. Breed them from Ghastly and Hateful.%n%nTo get their Blaze Rod drop, however, you'll need to place them in a biome that matches their default requirements. Sorry.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAI5Q.desc=Ah, here it is. This bee has been known to power whole civilizations. Placed in a top tier bee housing like an Alveary or Industrial Apiary, with appropriate frames, it can produce oil faster than some wells. In addition, you will get small amounts of Diesel fuel as well! Breed them from Oily and Distilled.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAI8Q.desc=sudo make me a sandwich. Or a bee that makes sandwich parts anyways. Breed them from Batty and Agrarian.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIdw.desc=Finally, Black Gold. The Oil bee, with proper... encouragement... can take care of all your power and chemical needs for quite some time. An alternate bee, Oily, requires less processing to get oil but has a longer breeding chain. It is below the Magical bees. Breed them from Coal and Sticky Resin.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIkw.desc=Zinc makes great early game item pipes when mixed into brass. Also, these bees have a small chance of producing Gallium combs, which is very useful for players needing to make circuits or SMD devices. These bees will require a Zinc block. Breed them from Tin and Iron.%n%nZinc Combs cannot be centrifuged. You now need to use a Chemical Reactor with some hydrochloric acid.%n%n[note]Breeder's Notes:%n%nYou probably only bred this as a stepping stone into the other metals. Nonetheless, that gallium is no joke! The queen will need to be jubilant for you to get those, so you need to match up its temperature and humidity band exactly. Your HUD will have a note when you are pointed at the apiary about if it's not jubilant. The default band is just NORMAL/NORMAL so any old plain/prairie kind of place will probably do.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAImQ.desc=Titanium from bees will make getting those LCRs and distillation towers a breeze. Hey, I rhymed! You'll need a block of Titanium for this bee. Breed them from Aluminium and Redstone.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAInA.desc=All that hatred had a purpose - to create this bee, capable of producing enormous power. As before, keep away from everything. This bee will require a block of Uranium. Breed them from Avenging and Platinum.%n%nTo actually get the combs you need to either find a biome with cold temperature and normal humidity or emulate these conditions.%n%n[note]With these combs and the iridium ones you can now make climate control units for modules in your industrial apiary![/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAItQ.name=Spirit
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAItQ.desc=The Spirit bee is the first bee to give you Soul Combs, necessary for Soulful Wax, used in many magical frames. Breed them from Aware and either Ethereal or Attuned.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAItg.name=Soul
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAItg.desc=The Soul bee has the highest chance of making Soul Combs, 20 percent. Well, except for Dreaming bees. Anyway, breed them from Aware and Spirit.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIug.name=Rejuvenating
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIug.desc=Rejuvenating bees must be bred within 25m of a node. They will slowly charge the nearest node. Breed them from Vis and Attuned.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIuw.name=Empowering
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIuw.desc=The Empowering bee will randomly add aspects to nearby nodes, allowing enormous power to build up. The best chance to breed them is during a full moon. Breed them from Rejuvenating and Vis.%n%n[note]The maximum node size was capped for a few versions, but that cap is now removed! Maybe go on the GTNH discord and praise Runakai for that. :)[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIvg.desc=Thaumium is pretty easy to make, but with this bee you can automate and get enormous quantities. It requires a block of Thaumium. Breed them from Edenic and Ignis.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIwQ.desc=The Thaumic Shards bee has a chance of giving you any shard propolis. It will require a Magical Forest biome. Breed them from Thaumium Dust and Aqua.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIxQ.name=Abandoned
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIxQ.desc=Abandoned are the next step up. Breed them from Oblivion and Nameless.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIxg.name=Draconic
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIxg.desc=The Draconic bee is required in order to get the dusts needed to recreate the Dragon Egg using magic. It must be bred in the End. Breed them from Imperial and Abandoned.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIxw.desc=The Wither bee will let you generate Wither skulls and small amounts of Nether star dust. It requires a block of Nether Star, and must be bred in the End. Breed them from Withering and Draconic.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIyA.name=Withering
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIyA.desc=Inflicts Withering all those who come near. Must be bred in the Nether. Chances are going to be low, so now would be the time to look for frames that increase mutation rates. Breed them from Demonic and Spiteful.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIyQ.name=Spiteful
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIyQ.desc=The sheer disdain this bee shows you is awe inspiring. Must be bred in the Nether. Don't walk around it without proper protection, it seems to laugh when you think about that. Breed them from Hateful and Infernal.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAM1g.name=D-O-B
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAM1g.desc=It is not the psychedelic drug kicking in. The NEI page is actually correct. You can get a lot of different stuff from this comb.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAM4Q.desc=Critical for your Ichor production.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAM4g.desc=Critical for your Ichor production.%n%n[note]You will need to breed through a bunch of elemental bees that don't have quests to actually get to it.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.EM4Z9io4QGSBNdSnymJNmg.name=Attuned
betterquesting.quest.EM4Z9io4QGSBNdSnymJNmg.desc=You're now getting into Magic Bees, and one of its mundane bee species is the Attuned species. These are scooped out of Deep Hives that you can find in the Overworld. These hives are a pain to find, so you should consider just buying hives with coins until you get a princess and a drone. However, if you are a real masochist or completionist try-hard, then here's some information about where they spawn:%n%n* From Y=1 to Y=25%n* In stone, surrounded on 5 sides. Not just vanilla stone.%n* In biomes tagged with one or more of:%n   * MOUNTAINS: Actual mountains may not count. It's the biome type that counts.%n      * Example: Canyon.%n   * HILLS: Again, actual hills don't count.%n      * Example: Snowy Coniferous Forest.%n   * MAGICAL: Unlike the others, they do have some ethereal aspect.%n      * Examples: Magical Forest is obvious, but also Cherry Blossom Grove counts.%n* Surrounded by a small redstone vein. This often fills any open space around them.%n%nThey also like to just kind of show up whatever-what-the-heck in other biomes. Our beekeeping intern found a Deep Hive in a Lush Desert:%n%nLush Desert [HOT, DRY, SAVANNA, LUSH, SANDY]%n%nYou can dump the biome data in NEI by clicking on the NEI options button (the wrench), then the Tools button, then the Data Dumps button, and finally the Dump button in the biomes category. This creates a "dumps" directory in the root folder of the modpack with a biome.csv inside of it. Any listed biome that has the tags of HILLS, MOUNTAINS, and/or MAGICAL can generate Deep Hives. You can feed these biomes into a Nature's Compass and see if there are any nearby.%n%nProspector's Scanners will pick up the little ore pockets for these (traces, small samples). If you had one of those end-game ones with a display, it would come up as a few red pixels. Larger ones are probably just regular ore veins. The ore finding wand doesn't do a good job from the surface. Chasing lava veins and tunnels helps. Ore veins filled with redstone will saturate either tool.%n%nOf course, just buying hives is the low-effort way.%n%n[note]Beekeeper's Notes:%n%nIf you get real bad luck and wind up with an ignoble princess, then just get a bunch of drones out of it and convert some other pristine princess afterwards. However, using base princesses will compel the bees to turn into the Common species. There are two choices:%n%n1. Use an Alveary with an Alveary Stabilizer to block mutations.%n2. Create a princess that doesn't line up with the Attuned species' breeding possibilities before starting.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.L38n8nAGSHGtZuBgrrf1mg.desc=Radioactive alert! The Uranus bee allows you to obtain resources from Uranus and its moons.
betterquesting.quest.Mrfvj2-bQ4SGkFsdtNzI1A.desc=The Moon bee allows you to obtain resources from the Moon.
betterquesting.quest.N0ZqNLJfSmaBKTNU7TbIAQ.name=Salt
betterquesting.quest.N0ZqNLJfSmaBKTNU7TbIAQ.desc=At this point, you may have noticed that these higher-tier metal combs can't be extracted with a centrifuge. Instead, you need to pass them through a chemical reactor with some hydrochloric acid. This will leave you in a pickle. Here you are, trying to reach post-scarcity, and now you're limited by chlorine.%n%nSpeaking of pickles, hydrochloric acid is kind of like a pickle, right? After all, you make both with salt! The salt bee is perfect for this. Well, the apatite bee line can get you some salt and also some phosphorus for phosphoric acid, but you have to start on ash bees first. Meanwhile, you'll likely take care of the salt bee's prerequisites on your way through getting all the major ores.%n%nBreed them from clay and aluminium bees on top of a block of salt.%n%nThey will produce salt combs, borax dust, slag combs, and trace lithium combs. The salt combs will require at least an MV-tier centrifuge, but at least it doesn't require processing with acid in a chemical reactor!%n%n[note]Breeder's Notes:%n%nThere are two challenges with this bee:%n%n1. The 5%% chance of mutation. You may consider trying the escritoire minigame to get a boost to this chance. If so, favor aluminium drones because you're probably on your way to the other bees derived from aluminium ancestry, and they all only have a 5%% chance anyways. They could all use a little boost.%n%n2. The humidity swing between clay and aluminium species. Clay bees want it wet, and both aluminium and salt bees want it completely arid. If you can't manipulate the climate or the tolerances of any of the bees, consider starting by plugging clay drones into a modest princess. This has a good chance to get you a clay princess that prefers a dryer climate. You can then do all your breeding exclusively in an arid biome.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.Ni8HtEo3SuGvXHXa7N7uoA.desc=This bee produces Barnarda dust.
betterquesting.quest.NzynzD7HQrmEAf7BFd2A2w.name=Glowstone
betterquesting.quest.NzynzD7HQrmEAf7BFd2A2w.desc=The Glowstone Princess isn't as picky as her peers. There are no breeding requirements besides the species being Gold and Redstone. Hooray!
betterquesting.quest.S8uP6eAqQ0Wc8ouKTvq2Hg.desc=This bee lets you produce molten Infinity in the DTPF!%n%n[note]Faster than an Infiniti drives on the road![/note]
betterquesting.quest.SlWASRc9TkKi7H0KiDPAlQ.name=Infernal
betterquesting.quest.SlWASRc9TkKi7H0KiDPAlQ.desc=Infernal bees are mundane: you get them from hives, and they have no ancestors.%n%nInfernal hives are in The Nether, surrounded by nether quartz. Avoid large nether quartz blobs in ore chunks. Instead, look for little pockets of nether quartz. Any ghast-infested, open area will show a few dabs of them. Alternately, if you're tunneling around, you'll inevitably bump into some of these small pockets.%n%nZombie pigmen will get mad if they spot you nibbling on their quartz, so consider just breaking away the netherrack around the quartz to see that it's a solid cluster that could surround a hive. If so, you are just one or two mining hammer swings away from a likely infernal hive.%n%nThere's another way to get these hives: §obuy them with coins! Ka-ching!%n§o§r%nTheir molten combs are nice for a mundane bee. They centrifuge down to refractory wax, which can be used for fireproof wood and refractory capsules.%n%n[warn]Infernal bees have an aggressive trait, so they'll damage entities--namely, you--when you are within their territory. You want an apiarist's suit before you start working with them. Alternately, if you set them up in an isolated spot, you can just run real fast. This isn't sustainable for all types of aggressive bees, by the way.[/warn]%n%n[note]Breeder's Notes: You can run these bees in the Overworld if you can find a hot/arid climate. When in doubt, place an apiary and look at what it claims the climate is in the upper right of its GUI. Even if the bee isn't jubilant, but you can get drones out of them for breeding. Then you don't have to run back and forth to The Nether to run a cycle with a fussy queen while cross-breeding.%n%nUse nether wart to keep them happy, and don't forget some soul sand!%n%nThey don't cross breed with other mundane bees into stuff like Common and Cultivated bees, so you can convert another mundane princess to an Infernal princess if you have the drones. Just take some care with this. For example, if you try this with an Arctic princess, you could wind up with an Infernal princess that needs a scorching/arid climate, but also needs snow to pollinate.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.V3flGsmJS0KdoLi63cw0lw.desc=The Trinium bee allows you to obtain Trinium.%n%n[note]There is no planet named Trinium, but this bee still provides a very useful ZPM material.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.VoQgq6UvTZmo3tpUIZs4Rg.name=Sunnarium
betterquesting.quest.VoQgq6UvTZmo3tpUIZs4Rg.desc=Not only does this bee produce more Glowstone than its parent species, but it's also capable of producing Sunnarium. However, this requires some technical progress: to breed this bee, you will need to place a Superconducting Coil Block beneath it.
betterquesting.quest.YHh-tuXHSCOng60JAB-u-w.desc=At last, you have reached the highest tier of bee evolution!%n%nKevlar is a very useful material from UV through UMV.%n%n[note]This bee lets you skip the many processing steps normally required to produce Kevlar.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.YVlqGPZBS8qCkkHlu1BDpg.name=Pyrotheum
betterquesting.quest.YVlqGPZBS8qCkkHlu1BDpg.desc=Blazing Pyrotheum is needed in large quantities to satisfy the unquenchable thirst of your Volcani. This Bee produces Pyrotheum Dust directly - all you need to do is fluid-extract it (after reaching this point in the breeding chain, of course).%n%nBreed these bees from Energy and Redstone Bees. They aren't picky about conditions, requiring only Hellish temperature. Yay!
betterquesting.quest.ZViN0XrYRwmXV0P60dODWg.desc=An infinite source of Oriharukon for producing Melodic Alloy.
betterquesting.quest._-pwbrvZQVu63dm85nDNsw.desc=You have finally obtained this new bee, and it is a game-changer! Its combs are especially useful for processing cosmic neutronium in the DTPF, making the recipe run twice as fast.
betterquesting.quest.akUvx1lTTwavvywH38qDtQ.desc=The Enceladus bee allows you to obtain resources found on Enceladus, one of Saturn's moons.
betterquesting.quest.bBpkCzjZSuimdCrJo3pBrA.desc=The Saturn bee allows you to obtain resources from Saturn.
betterquesting.quest.csd4ls5qRbSctFw65k9juw.desc=Barnarda F - Press F
betterquesting.quest.jvKBzB6tRpCQGlnboQxSAA.name=Gold
betterquesting.quest.jvKBzB6tRpCQGlnboQxSAA.desc=There are a plethora of ways to acquire gold, but here's one more for the dedicated apiarist. This breeding chain will eventually allow you to reach Sunnarium. You'll need a Block of Gold and a biome with a hot temperature. Breed them from Copper and Lead.
betterquesting.quest.m6IZ4sQnQrekZK6pkb5dOg.desc=The Pluto bee allows you to obtain resources from Pluto.%n%n[note]Pluto is Kruto![/note]
betterquesting.quest.mxb6nh1rQDS5d6WWov5ULQ.desc=The Neptune bee allows you to obtain resources from Triton and Proteus.
betterquesting.quest.noSgUClGTO6zMgENR9pwtw.name=Essentia
betterquesting.quest.noSgUClGTO6zMgENR9pwtw.desc=This bee produces nothing directly but instead sacrifices its lifetime to generate liquid essentia for all your magical needs. To do so, however, it requires an Apimancer's Drainer beneath its housing.%n%nThe speed at which the bee produces essentia is affected by its production speed. You have to right-click the drainer with a filled phial of the desired essentia to lock it to that type.%n%nYou can breed them from chaotic and ordered bees.%n%n§3You can also place up to 9 drainers beneath a single alveary as long as the blocks at the bottom are plain alveary blocks.
betterquesting.quest.oofRxeE1QBSGyew83metLg.desc=Even Elon Musk will envy you after you obtain this bee.
betterquesting.quest.rKrpOyRHRvSF7TeFSskG_A.name=Lapotron
betterquesting.quest.rKrpOyRHRvSF7TeFSskG_A.desc=This magnificent breed of Bee produces a whole plethora of useful resources, including endless amounts of Lapis, Energium, and Lapotron Dust. However, they are somewhat picky when it comes to breeding; you'll need Energium and Lapis Bees as parents, and the process must take place on the Moon under icy temperatures.
betterquesting.quest.riyWivmcQDypqdGXh3ZRbQ.desc=The Jupiter bee allows you to obtain resources from Jupiter.
betterquesting.quest.zMRva-UMR1-ZlN73PLW3Lw.desc=The Oberon bee allows you to obtain resources from Oberon.
betterquesting.quest.zpsHTWA-SfKTyAeJNUMZZA.desc=An Infinity Catalyst bee for your late-game Infinity needs.
betterquesting.questline.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.name=Hardcore End(er) Expansion
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACWg.name=Spatial Distortions
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACWg.desc=You detected a weird disturbance in the air around an Enderman. I suggest you try to steal some of their pearls and research them further.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACWw.name=Dimensional Chest
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACWw.desc=You've heard rumors that the Endermen had built laboratories in the End to invent new machines and weapons in order to attack the Overworld. One of their inventions is a chest, which is somehow linked to all instances of itself. Go and try to find one of those.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAD2g.name=Is This the End? No, it's the END Dimension
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAD2g.desc=You investigated the pearls, and managed to reactivate them to become eyes. This has shown you that the source of the disturbance seems to be coming out of the portal frames inside the strongholds, deep underground. They seem strangely drawn towards its mysterious depths. Perhaps they can be used to reactivate it?%n%nHint: Throwing Ender Eyes in the air in the Overworld will guide you to the nearest stronghold. From time to time Ender Eyes are destroyed in this process, so make extras. Try to do so in a place without obstructions so you can see where it went.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJLQ.name=Ender Towers
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJLQ.desc=Once you've explored a bit, you'll find large towering buildings that increase in difficulty as you go upwards, culminating in a dangerous boss fight.%n%nBe wary and bring strong protective armor!%n%nIf you are incredibly lucky, these towers can also offer rare items or blocks.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJLg.name=Welcome to the End!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJLg.desc=Welcome to the End! And more importantly, Hardcore Ender Expansion.%n%nIf you've already fought the Ender Dragon, you'll have noticed that the fight itself was challenging, far more than usual. Though much of the island may be destroyed, have no worry, there are plenty of End blobs out there for you to gather ore or endstone from.%n%nFirst, you will want to gather some End Powder, a key catalyst for most of HEE. Any means of flight is also highly recommended.%n%nHint: Press the P key (unless you rebound it) for a key list of information about HEE related stuff. Once you've looked through it you'll realize you need knowledge in order to unlock pages. Looking at blocks or items or certain things will also grant you knowledge. Consuming Knowledge Notes will also grant you knowledge points. Here are some for you to get started on. Good luck!%n%nYou can also search for the Adventurer's Diary for some lore if you want.%n%n[note]PS: Hold shift and whack the egg with a vanilla sword to get it to drop.[/note]%n%n[warn]The End has invisible rain, cover up your miners, and then complain on Discord.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJLw.name=Dragon Essence Altar
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJLw.desc=To create a Dragon Essence Altar, a player has to use Dragon Essence on the Basic Essence Altar (right-click the altar with the Essence).%n%nAfter that, the Altar will request 8 random items to be fed into it, one at a time.%n%nThe Dragon Essence Altar may request the following items: Obsidian, Stone Bricks, Map, Book, Bookshelf, Iron Bars, End Stone, Ender Pearl, Eye of Ender, Enderman Head.%n%nAfter this, the Altar will transform into a Dragon Essence Altar, and now you can store more Essence inside the Altar.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJMA.name=Essence Altar
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJMA.desc=This little enchanting table like-block doesn't do much on its own, but has two other separate paths that can be taken (the third has no uses currently) to accomplish different tasks.%n%nIt is up to you where and how you want your personal Essence Altar to be upgraded. Firstly and more importantly, make the Basic Essence Altar.%n%n[note]One of the upgrades uses Dragon Essence, but if you play on a public server and someone else killed the Dragon, that stuff can be difficult to come by without external help. Here's some to get you started.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJMQ.name=Find all the Ores in the End
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJMQ.desc=End Powder Ore:%nGenerated in the End in between End Stone at every height level. When the ore is mined with any type of pickaxe, it will drop one or two pieces of End Powder.%n%nEndium Ore:%nRare ore that starts to appear near Dungeon Towers, and gets more common the further you travel.%n%nIgneous Rock Ore:%nGenerated in the End in the Burning Mountains and sometimes in the Endstone Blobs. This block emits lava particles but does no damage to the player. When the ore is mined with an Iron Pickaxe or better, it will drop one Igneous Rock.%n%n[note]Note: the Fortune enchantment does not affect Igneous Rock Ore. However, the Silk Touch enchantment does work with this block. You can get better output with a Macerator.[/note]%n%nInstability Ore:%nGenerated in the End in the Biome Islands, especially common in the Fiery Mines. When the ore is mined with an Advanced Pickaxe, it has a 40%% chance to drop one Instability Orb, otherwise it breaks without providing any items.%n%n[note]Note: the Fortune enchantment increases the chance of getting an Instability Orb by 4%% per level, and the Silk Touch enchantment also works with this block. You can get better output with a Forge Hammer.[/note]%n%nStardust Ore:%nGenerated in the End in the Biome Islands. When the ore is mined with an Advanced Pickaxe, it has a chance to drop 0-4 pieces of Stardust. Even though this ore comes in clusters, two ore blocks from the same cluster can be generated away from each other, making Stardust Ore a rare resource which requires thorough exploration and mining.%n%n[note]Note: the Stardust Ore block has different textures on its sides.[/note]%n%nSphalerite: Often found floating in the open space around Endstone Blobs. You can macerate it for crushed normal Sphalerite.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJMg.name=Enhanced Brewing Stand
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJMg.desc=After the Altar creation is complete, a player has to place up to 8 matching solid blocks (of any kind) near the altar. These blocks require 1 block of air above them and no solid blocks touching them on the sides and diagonally. These blocks are the pedestals. The Dragon Essence Altar will project purple particles to all the pedestals connected to it.%n%nDropping an item onto the pedestal will place it there. After the item has been placed on top of the pedestal, the altar will start "infusing" the item using Dragon Essence stored in the altar itself. Adding more essence to the altar is done by right-clicking.%n%nInfusing makes items repair themselves (this does not work for items that require Energy), increases the level of existing enchantments (up to 4 enchantments per item) and can even add new enchantments.%n%nThere are two items in this mod that can be obtained only by Dragon Essence infusion:%n%nEnhanced Brewing Stand - by infusing a vanilla Brewing Stand, requires 20 pieces of Dragon Essence.%n%nTemple Caller - by infusing a vanilla Eye of Ender, requires 50 pieces of Dragon Essence. [warn]It's disabled though, so don't bother.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJMw.name=HEE Biome Compass
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJMw.desc=The Biome Compass is a special type of compass, which points to the nearest Biome Islands as long as one exists and the player is in the End. Right-clicking will scroll through all existing biomes.%n%nHolding the compass shows all biomes of the selected type as markers on the screen. The markers are small rectangles with the color of the selected biome. The rectangles also get bigger the closer you are to the island (they also disappear if you reach the island, and reappear when you leave it).%n%n[note]The Fiery Island is orange, the Enchanted Island (both variants) is purple, and the Infested Island is dark red.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJNA.name=Visit the (Enchanted) Laboratory Island
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJNA.desc=The Laboratory is a large structure used by Endermages to experiment with magical items from the End, and is also in the Enchanted biome found via the HEE Compass.%n%nThere are also regular chests with loot. Those can contain Obsidian Fragments and Auricion, amongst several other items.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJNQ.name=Energy Clusters and the Energy Wand
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJNQ.desc=Energy Clusters, the little glowing orbs you may have seen floating around, have different health levels, which affect the regeneration (or leaking) speed.%n%nClusters can be moved using an Energy Wand. Moving them too far or across dimensions can have negative effects on their health.%n%nBlocks that use Energy will take it from Clusters up to 16 blocks away, and from the environment if placed in the End.%n%nItems that use Energy automatically refill in the End, or can be used on a Cluster to start and stop draining the Energy.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJNg.name=Visit the (Enchanted) Homeland Island
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJNg.desc=A very flat biome with small amount of caves.%n%nThe Homeland variant has lakes of Ender Goo, piles of Falling Obsidian and a strange Obsidian road-like structure.%n%nYou can often find a Homeland Cache, a floating transparent cube that can be broken for some goodies, most importantly Arcane Shards. Endermen, Baby Endermen, and Ender Guardians spawn here.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJNw.name=Visit the Infested Island
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJNw.desc=The Infested Islands are mostly a flat biome with occasional hills, long caves and a decent amount of ores. There are 2 variations of the biome - Deep and Ravaged. Both of these variations contain Silverfish, Infested Bats and occasionally Endermen.%n%nThe Deep variation is massively populated with Spooky Trees that can have faces on them, which are how you get Ectoplasm. The ground has all types of infested plants, including Thorny Bushes.%n%nThe Ravaged variation has patches of infested plants and occasional Spooky Trees, but the most important feature is the Ravaged Dungeon which is an open gate to getting your Charms.%n%nAbout Infestation:%nSimply by standing on the Infested End Stone, the infestation level will rise. After leaving the area for several minutes, if the infestation level is low, it will reset and won't do any harm to the player.%n%nHowever, if the infestation level gets high enough, it will trigger one or more potion effects, which include weakness, slowness and mining fatigue, and if the player's level is severe, blindness, confusion and/or poison may take place as well. These effects cannot be cured using milk; however you can drink Infestation Remedy to shorten them.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOA.name=Visit the Fiery Island
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOA.desc=A Fire-oriented biome with huge mountains and a large amount of caves and ores. Apart from default ores, this biome also has common Igneous Rock ore. There are 2 variations of the biome - Scorching and Mine.%n%nThe Scorching variation has large blobs of cinder, streams and pools of Lava and Lilyfires. This is the only place where Fire Golems and Scorching Lenses spawn. Each island can contain a Dungeon Puzzle.%n%nThe Mine variation spawns Haunted Miners, which protect Resource Pits (holes with ores from the End and Lava) and long patches of Overworld ores. Not all Overworld ores are present on a single island, usually one or two random ores are missing.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOQ.name=Ghost Amulet
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOQ.desc=The Ghost Amulet (Impure) is an item that can only be obtained by throwing one Emerald, one String and one End Powder into Ender Goo.%n%nOnce you have that, you can purify it with a TC infusion, but that's expensive, so maybe the Ender Compendium has a more traditional way to infuse it.%n%nAs long as it stays anywhere in the inventory, it protects players from Forest Ghosts, and thus provides a way of acquiring Ectoplasm.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOg.name=Blank Gem
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOg.desc=The Blank Gem doesn't do anything on its own, but is used to create higher level Gems.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOw.name=Spatial Dash Gem
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJOw.desc=The Spatial Dash Gem is used for enderpearl-like teleportation.%n%nThe Spatial Dash Gem uses Energy and can be charged in an Energy Extraction Table. Right-clicking with the gem in hand sends a purple beam straight to where the player is aiming. When the beam hits a block, the player will be teleported to it. Maximum travel distance is 75 blocks horizontally. The teleportation doesn't hurt the player, unlike Ender Pearls.%n%nThe Spatial Dash Gem always tries to place the player on top of the block, even if the beam hits the side or bottom of it.%n%nThe Spatial Dash Gem can teleport the player through 7 solid blocks in a row, making the gem a good way of teleporting through cave walls and ceilings. If the wall is thicker than 7 blocks, the gem then tries to find 2 air blocks inside the wall. If the air blocks are not found, the player will be teleported into a wall, leading to suffocation.%n%n[note]A Spatial Dash Gem is also dropped by the Ender Eye mini-boss upon death.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJPA.name=Transference Gem
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJPA.desc=The Transference Gem is used to teleport to a marked location.%n%nThe Transference Gem uses Energy and can be charged in an Energy Extraction Table. Shift-right-clicking on a block with a Transference Gem in hand will link the gem to that block. The state of the gem itself will then switch to "Linked", as seen in its tooltip.%n%nAfter linking, the player can right-click with a Transference Gem in hand to teleport to the linked block, using some of the Energy stored in the gem.%n%nUsing F3+H to enable detailed item tooltips makes the Transference Gem show the exact coordinates and the dimension of the linked location.%n%nOnce the charge of the Transference Gem becomes lower than 44%%, negative effects will appear:%n%nDeflection - the player will be teleported to a random location instead of the linked block.%n%nVarious negative potion effects, the lower the charge is - the longer they will last:%n%nSlowness II%nNausea I%nWeakness II%nHunger I%n%nEndermen - Angry Endermen will spawn and attack the player.%n%nItem drop - a random amount of items in player's inventory will drop to the ground.%n%nStorm - will cause a 2-3 minute storm. This is the rarest effect.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJPQ.name=Gem Enchantment
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJPQ.desc=Spatial Dash Gems and Transference Gems can be enhanced in a similar manner, using End Powder and the enhancement item.%n%nRight-click the End Powder, choose an enchantment, and fill four End Powder and four Instability Orbs for instant teleport, four Lapis Lazuli for a longer teleport range, and four Endium Ingots to increase the capacity of the gem.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJPg.name=Advanced Gem Enchantment
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJPg.desc=Transference Gem and Spatial Dash Gems can be enhanced in a similar manner, using End Powder and the enhancement item.%n%nRight-click the End Powder, choose an enchantment, and fill with four End Powder and four Ectoplasm to teleport a monster, four Leather to teleport a whole group of players, and four Endium Ingots to increase the capacity of the gem.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJPw.name=Runes
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJPw.desc=There are 6 types of Runes found in the Ravaged Dungeons on the Infested Islands:%n%nPower%nVigor%nMagic%nDefense%nAgility%nVoid%n%nThe Void rune is less common than other types.%n%nRunes are used to create Charms, which are crafted in a Charm Pouch.%n%nBasic Runes increase attributes, such as strength, speed or health. Void Rune (gray) gives the Louse one of several special and extremely dangerous abilities.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQA.name=Charms
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQA.desc=Charms are player enchantments, used and crafted in the Charm Pouch.%nIf you are lucky you may find a pouch in the Dungeons.%n%nThis magical pouch allows creating, holding and activating Charms.%n%nSneaking and using the pouch activates or deactivates the Charms.%n%nOnly one pouch can be active at a time.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQQ.name=Hot Puzzle
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQQ.desc=Some of the islands have a Dungeon Puzzle inside them, usually near the surface and with a small cave leading to it. The dungeon consists of special blocks which the player can interact with by throwing Igneous Rock, causing a chain reaction during which the lit blocks will become unlit, unlit blocks will become lit and the walls will propagate the reaction into adjacent blocks.%n%nOnce all of the blocks are lit, a Fire Fiend is spawned below. It will make its way to the surface, breaking the dungeon in the process.%n%n[warn]Kill it with... well, probably not fire![/warn]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQg.name=Scorching Pickaxe
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQg.desc=The Scorching Pickaxe is a special type of pickaxe that smelts blocks and applies fortune effect to ores.%n%nIt only works on smeltable blocks and ores. Blocks that smelt into items are affected by fortune, including for example Iron Ore and Cactus.%n%nCompatible blocks are also mined much faster.%n%nGT Ores are not affected. You can find Vanilla Ores in the Twilight Forest inside Hollow Hills.%n%n[note]So basically, it's useless.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQw.name=Death Flowers
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQw.desc=The purple flowers found on top of Endstone Blobs are known as Death Flowers. They can be planted on End Stone, Dirt, Grass or inside Flower Pots.%n%nOutside the End, the flower will slowly decay, even if in a Flower Pot.%n%nAfter some time spent decaying, it starts to occasionally attract Angry Endermen.%n%nWhen the flower decays completely, it turns dark, propagates a massive amount of decay to nearby blocks and spawns an Energy Cluster.%n%nPartial decay can be healed a little using End Powder.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJRA.name=Living Matter
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJRA.desc=Living Matter is a combination of microorganisms used to craft curses.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJRQ.name=Silverfish Blood
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJRQ.desc=The Infested Island and its dungeons are swarming with Silverfish, and they have a 1 in 56 chance of leaving a drop of their blood behind after you kill them. Golden swords increase the chance to 1 in 14.%n%nThis rare material is used to brew Infestation Remedy, as well as in the crafting of some curses.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJRg.name=Infestation Remedy
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJRg.desc=Infestation Remedy is a drinkable (or throwable) item used to shorten effects of the Infestation.%n%nObtaining:%nThe Infestation Remedy is brewed in an Enhanced Brewing Stand, using Silverfish Blood as the brewing ingredient and an Awkward Potion.%n%nUsage:%nWhen drunk, the remedy will shorten each of the Infestation effects by 150 to 180 seconds.%n%nYou can make splash potions with gunpowder and 3 more End Powder as well.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJRw.name=Potion of Instability
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJRw.desc=The Potion of Instability is a special type of potion, which can be brewed by putting an Instability Orb into an Enhanced Brewing Stand with an Awkward Potion. The brewing process requires End Powder in the stand's special slot.%n%nUsage:%nAs any other potion, the Potion of Instability can be drunk (or thrown, if it's a splash potion). Unlike regular potions, this potion gives a random potion effect of random tier and duration to each player it affects. It can also apply potion effects which aren't available in vanilla potions, such as Jump or Hunger.%n%nTrivia:%nThe item tooltip contains ???, as opposed to a potion effect and duration.%n%nYou can make splash potions with gunpowder and 3 more End Powder as well.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJSA.name=Curses
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJSA.desc=A Curse is a magical powder that attaches itself to an area of blocks, a mob, or a player, crafted using living matter, End Powder and specific ingredients.%n%nIt can be either placed right on a block or an entity, or thrown. If it gets thrown into a group of entities, it will have a chance to hit more than one at the same time.%n%nCurses eventually disappear, but they can be made eternal by crafting them with stardust and an arcane shard. Eternal Curses will stay forever on blocks and mobs, and longer than normal Curses on players.%n%nCurses placed on blocks are only visible to the player who cast it, and for a short duration to players affected by it.%n%nGetting very close to a Curse makes it visible without having it affect you, but it requires extreme carefulness.%n%nIt is possible to remove Curses by using a Potion of Purity.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJSQ.name=Potion of Purity
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJSQ.desc=The Potion of Purity is a drinkable (or throwable) potion that removes Curses.%n%nObtaining:%nThis potion is brewed in an Enhanced Brewing Stand, using Ectoplasm as the brewing ingredient and an Awkward Potion.%n%nYou can make splash potions with gunpowder and 3 more End Powder as well.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJSg.name=Curse Amulet
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJSg.desc=The Curse Amulet reveals all nearby Curses placed on blocks and depletes Curses quicker when held.%n%nIt is created by throwing End Powder, Gold Ingot, Ectoplasm and String into Ender Goo.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJSw.name=Infused Brewing Stand
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJSw.desc=A Brewing Stand with one or more special effects (enhancements).%n%nYou can upgrade your Enhanced Brewing Stand with End Powder to modify it like other HEE items.%n%nYou can continue adding as many effects to one Brewing Stand as you want.%n%nEnhancements:%nTier (Ectoplasm)%nYour potion can have a higher tier and a longer potion duration than vanilla ones. (Tier IV is up to 12 mins)%n%nSpeed (Igneous Rock)%nIncreases the speed of the Brewing Stand.%n%nCost (Emerald)%nReduces the cost of End Powder used in a brewing cycle.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJTA.name=TNT Enchantments
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJTA.desc=Enhanced TNT is a special version of vanilla TNT with one or more special effects (enhancements).%n%nThe way to make enhanced TNT is to right-click with End Powder in your hand to modify your TNT. You can continue adding as many effects to one TNT as you want.%n%nEnhancements:%nNo block damage (Feather)%nTNT explodes with no block damage.%n%nNo Entity damage (Slime)%nTNT explodes with no entity damage.%n%nExtra Damage (Gunpowder)%nTNT explodes with extra damage.%n%nTrap (Redstone)%nTNT explodes when a hostile mob touches or walks over the TNT block.%n%nNo Clip (Enderpearls)%nTNT falls through solid blocks and explodes after a few seconds.%n%nFire (Igneous Rock)%nTNT explodes with a big fire spread.%n%nNo Fuse (Redstone Torch)%nTNT explodes immediately.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJTQ.name=Enderpearl Enchantments
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJTQ.desc=Enhanced Ender Pearls are a special version of vanilla Ender Pearls with one or more special effects (enhancements).%n%nThe way to make enhanced pearls is to right-click with End Powder in your hand to modify your ender pearl. You can continue adding as many effects to one pearl as you want.%n%nThese effects are useful when throwing the pearl, for pearl teleportation effects.%n%nNatural occurrence:%nIt is possible to find pearls with random effects in a Dungeon Tower's loot chests.%n%nEnhancements:%nNo fall damage (Wool)%nUpon the pearl's landing, the player will not receive any fall damage.%n%nNo gravity (Feather)%nThe pearl will not follow the rules of gravity, which makes it possible to throw it straight up. After 10 seconds of flight, the pearl is automatically destroyed without any teleportation or fall damage.%n%nIncreased range (String)%nUnlike the no gravity effect, the pearl will fall down due to gravity, but will do so 25%% slower. If the pearl has the no gravity effect too, it will override this effect.%n%nDouble speed (Gold Nugget)%nIncreases the pearl's speed by a factor of 2, but won't change the flight trajectory. This can be helpful if you are in a bad situation (fell in lava, swarm of mobs around...) and need to be saved very quickly. In combination with the riding effect, you may notice slight stuttering on a server.%n%nExplosive (Gunpowder)%nUpon landing, the pearl will explode with radius of 2.7 (TNT has radius of 4). This will not harm the thrower as long as they are far enough from the landing spot.%n%nFreeze (Snowball)%nThe pearl will freeze mobs and players within 5 blocks of the landing spot for at least 4 seconds. Just as with the explosive effect, this will not affect the thrower unless they throw the pearl close to them, or have the riding effect applied. This effect is also followed by ice cracking sound and snow particles.%n%nRiding (Lead)%nThe thrower will "ride" the pearl to its destination. During the ride, if another pearl with this effect is thrown, the previous pearl will destroy itself and deal fall damage (unless No fall damage effect is applied).%n%nTrivia:%nThe Enhanced Ender Pearls can still be used for crafting an Eye of Ender.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJTg.name=Infused Altar
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJTg.desc=You can upgrade your Altar with one or more special effects (enhancements).%n%nThe way to make an enhanced Altar is to right-click your Altar with End Powder in your hand, then supplying End Powder and the enhancement material in the UI. You can continue adding as many effects to one Altar as you want.%n%nEnhancements:%nRange (Block of Lapis)%nIncrease the range at which an item can be infused by the Altar.%n%nSpeed (Block of Redstone)%nIncrease the working speed of the Altar.%n%nEfficiency (Block of Emerald)%nReduce the cost of Dragon Essence used by Altar recipes.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJTw.name=Curse Master
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJTw.desc=Curse of Teleportation%nTeleport Entities around randomly.%n%nCurse of Confusion%nConfuses mobs. Creepers just explode and have no fuse time or mobs fight each other.%n%nCurse of Tranquillity%nPrevent mobs from attacking you. Doesn't work on Boss mobs.%n%nCurse of Slowness%nInflicts slow on mobs.%n%nCurse of Weakness%nInflicts weakness on mobs.%n%nCurse of Blindness%nInflicts blindness on mobs.%n%nCurse of Death%nDoes 1.5 magical damage to mobs. Mobs bleed for a while and lose health.%n%nCurse of Decay%nItems and armor get damaged over time.%n%nCurse of Vampire%nMobs become sensitive to sunlight and take more damage.%n%nCurse of Rebound%nAdds reflection damage to a mob.%n%nCurse of Loss%nItems will be removed out of your inventory and get destroyed or fall on the ground.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJUA.name=Charm Master
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJUA.desc=You think you're charming? Craft all these Charms to be the true Master of Charms.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJUQ.name=Master Grinder
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJUQ.desc=After conquering most of the content inside the End, it is time for a Master Quest.%n%nBring forth and slay the following and you shall receive some moderately great loot.
